From 5975be1c35864af352328e961717a14375b1fa7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:36:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] virtio/gpu: a dxmt context in place of rutabaga_gfx

MacNeutron's EAC microVM forwards DXMT's Metal calls from the guest to the
host through a virtio-gpu context type, dxmt (capset 24). rutabaga_gfx needs
virglrenderer and keeps its component traits private, so a stand-in crate,
src/rutabaga_dxmt (patched in for rutabaga_gfx), implements the API subset
the gpu device uses: dxmt contexts, HOST3D blobs as 16 KiB-aligned host
memory, command buffers and fences handed to callbacks the VM host registers
(mn_dxmt_set_ops, mn_dxmt_fence_done). Without them fences complete at once.

The macOS blob map refuses an offset off a host page (Hypervisor.framework
maps whole pages), and GpuDevice::without_display builds a device without
scanouts or virgl capsets, so the device offers one capset: the context's.
